Z||000009||Oreif||12-18-2001||02:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>Isn't that an Illinois plate? Oreif, check that out for us!! Where IS that car??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The movie was filmed here in Illinois. The car was auctioned off after the movie was done. I wouldn't have a clue how to locate it. Anyone have a VIN?<BR>If they make a movie here occasionally they auction the cars off at the end. There is a guy who bought the 50/51 Chevy used in a Steve McQueen movie. (Forgot the name, he played a bounty hunter named "Pappy Doyle")<BR>The guy had it in his Restauraunt in Oak Lawn, IL many years ago.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||kenny86GT||12-18-2001||03:21 AM||||I know where that Ferris Bueller Fiero is, it's resting peacefully in Victorville, Ca. <BR>I know because, while I was in the Marine Corps stationed in Hawaii, they have a "Hollywood Hot Rod" show every year on the island of Oahu. The guy that had it was from Victorville. He said he paid only $3,000.00 for it. The car was originally borrowed from a car lot in Calumet City? After it registered a mear 6 1/2 miles on it, it was auctioned. This guy bought it, loaded it on a trailer and it has never seen the road at more than 1MPH since. The guy's name is Gary DeLarson(pretty sure).||||reg||3
