Z||000013||ProudGT||12-18-2001||10:27 AM||||There were two Fieros.<BR>The shots of the Fiero in the driveway above were actually shot on Country Club Drive (between Terrylynn Place and Marion Way) in Long Beach, California. That was the California Fiero. It was famous. <BR>The shots of Jeanie driving the Fiero at  school were filmed outside Glenbrook North High School in Northbrook, Illinois. The "Chicago" film crew found a matching Fiero at Levin Pontiac in Chicago Heights, Illinois (near Calumet City) and "borrowed" it for one day. It was not famous.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000014||neohio||12-18-2001||10:38 AM||||Hey Kenny and Haagster, I didn't know there was anyone on here from my area..I live in Akron..do you guys know where there are any junkyards that have any Fieros?? I have looked all over the place and found 1 and it was totally stripped to the frame..Oh.wheres there a place to get a wheel alignment? everywhere I have went they wont touch fieros..they say they can't align them and I need to take it to a pontiac dealership and get it done<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://osamayomomma.hypermart.net/files/osama_running.gif"> <BR>You can run, but you can't hide!||||reg||1
Z||000015||2M4 Dale||12-18-2001||12:19 PM||||North Central Tire on Clairmont Ave. in Ashland , Ohio does a fine job of Fiero alignment..I've got them broke in !!! Thier phone number is : 419-289-0123...ask for Darrell and tell him Dale Starcher sent Ya !||||reg||4
Z||000016||Haagster||12-18-2001||12:20 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by neohio:<BR><B>Hey Kenny and Haagster, I didn't know there was anyone on here from my area..I live in Akron..do you guys know where there are any junkyards that have any Fieros?? <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I went to school in Doylestown (20 years ago).  Haven't lived there for probably 15.  Sorry, but the last time I was in the area, I had to ask directions about Montrose (used to be a drive-in theater and little else).  I couldn't get around Akron University because they closed Buchtel Avenue (it was opened when I was a student there).  As for junk yards, the ones that I used to hit all of the time (couldn't tell you about any potential Fieros) were Kenmore Blvd heading toward Barberton, Eastern Road in Doylestown, Rte 604 south of Rittman, and one down the road from Barberton's drive-in theater (if it's still there) (Cleveland - Massilon Road).  The best one though, was right off of Rte21 in Massillon.  It was a little far to drive, but THEY always had what I was looking for - But then again, that was years ago.  Sorry...<p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Haagster||12-18-2001||12:38 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2M4 Dale:<BR><B>North Central Tire on Clairmont Ave. in Ashland , Ohio does a fine job of Fiero alignment..I've got them broke in !!! Thier phone number is : 419-289-0123...ask for Darrell and tell him Dale Starcher sent Ya !</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is Dorlos Pizza still open in Ashland?  They were the WORST pizza in the world back in the 80s.  A friend (who worked at Will Research) took us to Dorlos for their "all you can eat" pizza.  1/2 slice was more than enough. <P>*** Not to get off the subject ***<p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||My7Fieros||12-18-2001||01:46 PM||||Anybody notice the tag? "TBC" for "The Breakfast Club"...same guy did those movies as well as others. (And of course Ive got a brain fart and cant remember his name..doh!). I think there was a thread about this a while back....I believe the moms station wagon in the movie has a personalized tag to which stands for another one of his movies......somebody on here knows, like I said, I think there was a thread about this a while back.||||reg||1
Z||000019||2M4 Dale||12-18-2001||02:32 PM||||Yep Dorlos is still open and the pizza is still terrible !!!<P>HAHAHA...funny how small a world it is.<P>The junk yard on 604 is still there...barely<P>Beehites on Eastern Rd is about to go out of business and the one down the street from Magic City Drive Inn has been gone for years !!!<P>Oh and the Drive Inn Theater in Montrose no longer exists either.....progress 'eh lol<P>We lived in Doylestown about 23 years ago.<P>I'm from Norton originally.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Haagster||12-18-2001||02:36 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Anybody notice the tag? "TBC" for "The Breakfast Club"...same guy did those movies as well as others. (And of course Ive got a brain fart and cant remember his name..doh!). </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>John Hughes:  His movies include:  National Lampoon's Class Reunion (1982) National Lampoon's Vacation (1983) Mr. Mom (1983) Sixteen Candles (1984) Weird Science (1985) National Lampoon's European Vacation (1985)  The Breakfast Club (1985) Pretty in Pink (1986) Ferris Bueller's Day Off (1986) Some Kind of Wonderful (1987) She's Having a Baby (1988) Planes, Trains & Automobiles (1987) The Great Outdoors (1988) Uncle Buck (1989) National Lampoon's Christmas Vacation (1989) Home Alone (1990) Dutch (1991) Curly Sue (1991) Career Opportunities (1991) Only the Lonely (1991) Home Alone 2: Lost in New York (1992) Beethoven (1992) Dennis the Menace (1993) Beethoven's 2nd (1993) Miracle on 34th Street (1994) Baby's Day Out (1994) 101 Dalmatians (1996) Home Alone 3 (1997) Vegas Vacation (1997) Flubber (1997) Reach the Rock (1998) Beethoven's 3rd (2000)  Just Visiting (2001) New Port South (2001) Beethoven's 4th (2002) The Chambermaid (2002) <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||Haagster||12-18-2001||02:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2M4 Dale:<BR><B>Beehites on Eastern Rd is about to go out of business and the one down the street from Magic City Drive Inn has been gone for years !!!<P>Oh and the Drive Inn Theater in Montrose no longer exists either.....progress 'eh lol<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Like I said, it's been a while since I was in the area...  I went to school with one of the Beehite (sp?) kids, and that yard was in bad shape then.  The yard by Magic City used to be a pretty good source for Rustang parts (friend had a '71 back then).  I did see all of the new construction (ok, new to me) around Montrose the last time I was there (3-4 years ago).  I remember going to the old flea market at that drive-in when I was 5 or 6 years old.  Now, I couldn't recognize the place...  Like you say, progress.||||reg||1
