Z||000027||ProudGT||12-19-2001||04:29 PM||||Hey kenny86GT. You mentioned the guy also had "the original Blues Mobile"<BR>In Ferris Bueller's Day Off, there were only two Fieros. <BR>In the 1980 Blues Brothers there were 13 Dodge Monacos .<BR>Just like the Fieros in FBDO, there were "Chicago" Bluesmobiles and a "California" Bluesmobile. The 12 "Chicago" cars were crashed and smashed so often only one car with the best bits/pieces was shipped to the soundstage in California to join a 13th that was only a shell. During the Shopping Center filming, 5 Bluesmobiles were completely destroyed and were left to go to the landfill along with the remains of the Shopping Center. There were more than 200 cars that never saw the end of filming in Chicago, mostly fake City of Chicago Police Cars. These were all hauled to a junkyard in Hammond, Indiana and crushed. There are about 60 Bluesmobiles claiming to be "the original" but only one that could actually make the claim, now lost after being sold by a guy named Jim Post. <BR>They were thinking for Blues Brothers 2000, and that "official" Bluesmobile is at Universal Studios.<BR>Didn't mean to change the subject of this thread, but couldn't help but make the reply. ||||reg||11
Z||000028||kenny86GT||12-20-2001||03:00 AM||||ProudGT... Didn't say he HAD the original, just said it was parked next to what was supposed to be the original. The Blues Mobile was owned by some other guy. And he had some pics of it setting on the lot at Universal. Granted I can't vouch for his integrity, all I can say is that I saw these two cars and I just assumed they were IT! But I really do appreciate the Film and TV trivia. I love that kinda stuff. <P>------------------<BR>Those who are crazy enough to think they can change the world...DO! Kenny Starcher.||||reg||1
